problems.problem:
Denote by $S(x)$ the sum of the digits of a natural number $x$. Solve the equations:

a) $x+S(x)+S(S(x))=1993$;

b) $x+S(x)+S(S(x))+S(S(S(x)))=1993$.

A convex quadrilateral $ABCD$ and a point $O$ inside it are given. It is known that $\angle AOB=\angle COD=120^\circ$, $AO=OB$ and $CO=OD$. Let $K$, $L$ and $M$ be the midpoints of the segments $AB$, $BC$ and $CD$ respectively. Prove that

a) $KL=LM$;

b) the triangle $KLM$ is equilateral.

$2006$ schoolchildren took part in an olympiad. It turned out that the schoolboy Vasya solved only one of all six problems, and that the number of participants who solved

• at least $1$ problem is $4$ times the number of those who solved at least $2$;

• at least $2$ problems is $4$ times the number of those who solved at least $3$;

• at least $3$ problems is $4$ times the number of those who solved at least $4$;

• at least $4$ problems is $4$ times the number of those who solved at least $5$;

• at least $5$ problems is $4$ times the number of those who solved all $6$.

How many schoolchildren did not solve a single problem?
